1
00:00:01,543 --> 00:00:02,753
Hey, Rach, listen.

2
00:00:02,753 --> 00:00:04,839
Did you know
that during pregnancy

3
00:00:04,839 --> 00:00:07,716
your fingers swell
up to twice their size

4
00:00:07,716 --> 00:00:09,092
and never go back?

5
00:00:10,469 --> 00:00:11,846
Oh, my God.

6
00:00:11,846 --> 00:00:13,180
Let me see that.

7
00:00:14,222 --> 00:00:15,683
You fall for it every time.

8
00:00:17,810 --> 00:00:19,353
Hey.

9
00:00:19,353 --> 00:00:21,355
Look, I brought you
my old maternity clothes.

10
00:00:21,355 --> 00:00:23,106
Oh, Pheebs, that's so sweet.

11
00:00:23,106 --> 00:00:26,067
Oh, those are so cute.

12
00:00:26,067 --> 00:00:27,486
And look.

13
00:00:27,486 --> 00:00:30,322
See how they expand
as the baby grows?

14
00:00:30,322 --> 00:00:32,366
And then, after
the baby's born

15
00:00:32,366 --> 00:00:34,827
they're great for
shoplifting melons.

16
00:00:38,038 --> 00:00:39,331
Oh, good, you're all here.

17
00:00:39,331 --> 00:00:41,834
Okay, Thanksgiving
tomorrow, 4:00.

18
00:00:41,834 --> 00:00:42,877
Oh.

19
00:00:42,877 --> 00:00:44,378
And guess who I invited?

20
00:00:44,378 --> 00:00:46,463
Remember that guy,
Will Colbert from high school?

21
00:00:46,463 --> 00:00:47,756
No.

22
00:00:47,756 --> 00:00:49,424
He was in Ross's class.

23
00:00:49,424 --> 00:00:52,051
Marching band,
was kind of overweight.

24
00:00:52,051 --> 00:00:53,804
Well, really overweight.

25
00:00:53,804 --> 00:00:55,973
I mean, I was his thin friend.

26
00:00:57,975 --> 00:00:59,977
Wow, I don't
remember him.

27
00:00:59,977 --> 00:01:01,311
Honey, are you sure
you're not talking

28
00:01:01,311 --> 00:01:02,771
about your
imaginary boyfriend?

29
00:01:02,771 --> 00:01:06,817
No, that was Jarod.

30
00:01:06,817 --> 00:01:10,779
Wow. Haven't thought
about him in a long time.

31
00:01:12,573 --> 00:01:15,325
Anyway, Will's...
Will's here on business

32
00:01:15,325 --> 00:01:16,535
and he didn't haves
a place to go

33
00:01:16,535 --> 00:01:17,536
so I invited him here.

34
00:01:17,536 --> 00:01:19,038
Well, that's nice.

35
00:01:19,038 --> 00:01:20,622
Oh, and by the way
he's lost a bunch of weight.

36
00:01:20,622 --> 00:01:22,958
I mean, he looks good.

37
00:01:22,958 --> 00:01:25,711
Okay, I mean really,
really gorgeous.

38
00:01:25,711 --> 00:01:27,046
( clearing throat )

39
00:01:29,757 --> 00:01:31,341
I still love Chandler.

40
00:01:31,341 --> 00:01:33,677
Wouldn't hurt you
to say it once in a while.

41
00:01:35,804 --> 00:01:38,599
All right, okay, also,
just so you'll know--

42
00:01:38,599 --> 00:01:39,975
I'm not going to make
a turkey this year.

43
00:01:39,975 --> 00:01:41,769
What?
Well...

44
00:01:41,769 --> 00:01:42,895
Phoebe doesn't
eat turkey.

45
00:01:42,895 --> 00:01:44,271
Phoebe!

46
00:01:44,271 --> 00:01:47,608
Turkeys are beautiful,
intelligent animals.

47
00:01:47,608 --> 00:01:50,694
No, they're not. They're ugly,
and stupid and delicious.

48
00:01:52,487 --> 00:01:55,282
All right, it's not just Phoebe.
Will's still on a diet.

49
00:01:55,282 --> 00:01:56,867
Chandler doesn't eat
Thanksgiving food

50
00:01:56,867 --> 00:01:59,828
and Rachel's having
her aversion to poultry.

51
00:01:59,828 --> 00:02:02,039
She is?
Yeah. Don't you remember I had
to leave the room the other day

52
00:02:02,039 --> 00:02:03,624
when you had that
roast chicken?

53
00:02:03,624 --> 00:02:05,125
Yeah, but I thought
that was just 'cause

54
00:02:05,125 --> 00:02:06,460
I put the whole thing on my hand

55
00:02:06,460 --> 00:02:08,420
and made it walk
across the table.

56
00:02:09,755 --> 00:02:11,214
Anyway, it just
doesn't seem worth it

57
00:02:11,214 --> 00:02:13,132
to make a whole turkey
for just three people, okay?

58
00:02:13,132 --> 00:02:15,094
It's a lot of work.

59
00:02:15,094 --> 00:02:17,638
But you got to have
turkey on Thanksgiving.

60
00:02:17,638 --> 00:02:20,891
I mean, Thanksgiving with
no turkey is like, like...

61
00:02:20,891 --> 00:02:22,851
Fourth of July
with no apple pie

62
00:02:22,851 --> 00:02:26,521
or, or Friday
with no two pizzas.

63
00:02:26,521 --> 00:02:28,482
All right, fine, if it
means that much to you

64
00:02:28,482 --> 00:02:30,233
but there's going to
be a ton left over.

65
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:33,612
No, there won't. I promise
I will finish that turkey.

66
00:02:33,612 --> 00:02:34,989
All right, you're telling me

67
00:02:34,989 --> 00:02:36,657
you can eat almost
an entire turkey

68
00:02:36,657 --> 00:02:37,741
in one sitting?

69
00:02:37,741 --> 00:02:38,742
That's right.

70
00:02:38,742 --> 00:02:41,244
'Cause I'm a Tribbiani.

71
00:02:41,244 --> 00:02:43,831
This is what we do.

72
00:02:43,831 --> 00:02:45,707
I mean, we may not
be great thinkers

73
00:02:45,707 --> 00:02:48,002
or world leaders.

74
00:02:48,002 --> 00:02:50,253
We don't read a lot
or run very fast

75
00:02:50,253 --> 00:02:51,755
but, damn it, we can eat!

76
00:02:58,929 --> 00:03:03,934
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

77
00:03:03,934 --> 00:03:06,353
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

78
00:03:06,353 --> 00:03:08,605
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

79
00:03:08,605 --> 00:03:13,443
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

80
00:03:13,443 --> 00:03:15,779
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

81
00:03:15,779 --> 00:03:19,033
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

82
00:03:19,033 --> 00:03:22,285
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

83
00:03:22,285 --> 00:03:25,789
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

84
00:03:33,088 --> 00:03:34,506
Isn't it weird
to think about

85
00:03:34,506 --> 00:03:35,924
how next year
at this time

86
00:03:35,924 --> 00:03:37,676
there'll be a little baby
at the table?

87
00:03:41,638 --> 00:03:42,973
Rachel's

88
00:03:42,973 --> 00:03:44,183
but good to know
where you're at.

89
00:03:46,351 --> 00:03:47,644
Hey!
Hey.

90
00:03:47,644 --> 00:03:49,688
Happy Thanksgiving.
You, too.

91
00:03:49,688 --> 00:03:51,982
Anything I can do to help?
Actually there is.

92
00:03:51,982 --> 00:03:53,608
Chandler usually helps me
with this, but he's really
into the game,

93
00:03:53,608 --> 00:03:55,276
so I don't want to bother him.

94
00:03:55,276 --> 00:03:57,863
Could you help me
fold these napkins?
Sure.

95
00:03:57,863 --> 00:04:00,157
I'm going to go across the hall
to check on the yams.
Okay.

96
00:04:00,157 --> 00:04:02,159
Oh, no, no, no, sweetie.

97
00:04:02,159 --> 00:04:04,452
No, not like that.

98
00:04:04,452 --> 00:04:05,662
We're not
at a barn dance.

99
00:04:07,831 --> 00:04:09,416
You want to fold them
like swans

100
00:04:09,416 --> 00:04:11,668
like I showed you
at Christmastime, remember?

101
00:04:11,668 --> 00:04:13,921
Yeah, it all just came
screaming back to me.

102
00:04:17,841 --> 00:04:19,051
So, how's the game?

103
00:04:19,051 --> 00:04:20,802
I have no idea.

104
00:04:20,802 --> 00:04:22,387
What?

105
00:04:22,387 --> 00:04:23,972
Yeah. I'm just pretending
to watch the game

106
00:04:23,972 --> 00:04:26,225
so I don't have
to help out with stuff.

107
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:29,561
I don't believe you.

108
00:04:29,561 --> 00:04:31,688
That is... brilliant.

109
00:04:33,607 --> 00:04:35,734
And Monica has no idea?
Nope.

110
00:04:35,734 --> 00:04:38,862
Every once in a while, I just
yell and scream stuff at the TV.

111
00:04:39,905 --> 00:04:42,074
Hey! Oh, hey!

112
00:04:44,409 --> 00:04:45,786
Is your team winning, hon?

113
00:04:45,786 --> 00:04:47,495
Yeah, Anderson
just scored again.

114
00:04:48,538 --> 00:04:50,040
There's no Anderson.

115
00:04:52,793 --> 00:04:55,087
Well, I want to get in on this.

116
00:04:55,087 --> 00:04:57,547
Hey, Mon, I don't think
I can help you after all.

117
00:04:57,547 --> 00:04:59,633
I didn't realize
this game was on.

118
00:04:59,633 --> 00:05:01,760
Oh. I didn't know
you liked football.

119
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:05,597
Well, normally I don't,
but, you know...

120
00:05:05,597 --> 00:05:07,682
Green Bay is playing.

121
00:05:07,682 --> 00:05:09,101
You like Green Bay?

122
00:05:09,101 --> 00:05:11,311
Well, it's only,
like, my favorite bay.

123
00:05:12,980 --> 00:05:15,149
( knocking )

124
00:05:17,985 --> 00:05:19,820
Hey.
Hey.

125
00:05:24,032 --> 00:05:25,951
Happy Thanksgiving.
Oh, thanks.

126
00:05:25,951 --> 00:05:27,953
God, Will, I'm so
glad that you came.

127
00:05:27,953 --> 00:05:29,329
You look great.

128
00:05:29,329 --> 00:05:30,371
You must have
lost, like...

129
00:05:30,371 --> 00:05:32,332
150 pounds.

130
00:05:32,332 --> 00:05:35,210
Yeah, I'm going to be
in one of those Subway
sandwich commercials.

131
00:05:37,004 --> 00:05:38,672
A pie.
All right.

132
00:05:38,672 --> 00:05:41,382
It's no fat, it's no
sugar, it's no dairy.

133
00:05:41,382 --> 00:05:43,093
It's no good.
Throw it out.

134
00:05:44,178 --> 00:05:45,470
You want to meet
some people?

135
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:47,264
This is, uh, this is
my husband Chandler.

136
00:05:47,264 --> 00:05:48,556
Chandler, this is Will.
Hi.

137
00:05:48,556 --> 00:05:50,391
Oh, hey. I'd shake your hand

138
00:05:50,391 --> 00:05:53,603
but I'm really into the game.

139
00:05:53,603 --> 00:05:55,230
Plus, I think it would
be better for my ego

140
00:05:55,230 --> 00:05:58,108
if we didn't stand
right next to each other.

141
00:06:00,235 --> 00:06:01,236
This is Phoebe.

142
00:06:01,236 --> 00:06:02,237
Hi.

143
00:06:02,237 --> 00:06:03,738
Hey.

144
00:06:03,738 --> 00:06:05,032
Wow.

145
00:06:05,032 --> 00:06:08,160
( gasps )

146
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:09,661
Well done.

147
00:06:10,996 --> 00:06:12,539
Want to give me a hand?
Sure.

148
00:06:12,539 --> 00:06:14,457
Monica, I can't get over
how great you look.

149
00:06:14,457 --> 00:06:15,876
You look stunning.

150
00:06:15,876 --> 00:06:18,419
You look incredible, too.
You're so fit.

151
00:06:18,419 --> 00:06:20,714
I'm watching the game,
but I'm not deaf.

152
00:06:22,632 --> 00:06:25,093
Oh, um, I meant to tell
you-- Ross is coming.

153
00:06:25,093 --> 00:06:27,512
Ross is coming?
Great. I love Ross.

154
00:06:27,512 --> 00:06:29,264
Good, and Rachel Green, too.

155
00:06:30,307 --> 00:06:33,434
Ooh.

156
00:06:33,434 --> 00:06:34,435
Is there a problem?

157
00:06:34,435 --> 00:06:36,730
No. Uh...

158
00:06:36,730 --> 00:06:38,857
It's okay. It's just, uh...

159
00:06:38,857 --> 00:06:41,609
God, I hated her.

160
00:06:41,609 --> 00:06:42,610
What?

161
00:06:42,610 --> 00:06:43,945
Yeah, I hated her.

162
00:06:43,945 --> 00:06:47,115
She was horrible to me
in high school...

163
00:06:47,115 --> 00:06:49,076
but, hey,
it was a long time ago.

164
00:06:49,076 --> 00:06:50,535
I'm in a good place.

165
00:06:50,535 --> 00:06:52,287
It might be actually fun
to see her again.

166
00:06:52,287 --> 00:06:53,663
Okay.

167
00:06:53,663 --> 00:06:55,498
Got any cakes
or cookies or something?

168
00:06:58,335 --> 00:07:01,546
No, Will. No.

169
00:07:01,546 --> 00:07:03,131
You know, it's been a while
since we've screamed something.

170
00:07:03,131 --> 00:07:04,132
Maybe we should.

171
00:07:04,132 --> 00:07:05,342
Oh, okay.

172
00:07:05,342 --> 00:07:07,677
Oh, come on!
No!

173
00:07:07,677 --> 00:07:10,430
Damn you, ref!
You burn in hell!

174
00:07:14,809 --> 00:07:16,937
Hey, what are
you doing?

175
00:07:16,937 --> 00:07:19,689
You got to save room.
You've got almost
an entire turkey to eat.

176
00:07:19,689 --> 00:07:21,942
Let me explain to you
how the human body works.

177
00:07:23,526 --> 00:07:26,280
I have to warm up
my stomach first.

178
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:28,865
Eating chips is like stretching.

179
00:07:28,865 --> 00:07:30,450
Okay.

180
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:32,786
Yeah. Don't worry,
Tribbianis never get full.

181
00:07:32,786 --> 00:07:34,329
I actually know what
you're talking about

182
00:07:34,329 --> 00:07:35,455
and I'm here to tell you
something, friend.

183
00:07:35,455 --> 00:07:36,748
You can eat and eat and eat

184
00:07:36,748 --> 00:07:38,750
but nothing will ever
fill that void.

185
00:07:41,669 --> 00:07:43,422
Who the hell is this guy?

186
00:07:44,505 --> 00:07:45,840
Will, from
high school. Joey.

187
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:47,675
Oh, hey.
Hello.

188
00:07:47,675 --> 00:07:48,718
Will!
Ross.

189
00:07:48,718 --> 00:07:50,137
Hey, you came.

190
00:07:50,137 --> 00:07:52,764
Man, you look incredible.

191
00:07:52,764 --> 00:07:54,266
Hot stuff!

192
00:07:56,101 --> 00:07:57,894
"Hot stuff"?

193
00:07:57,894 --> 00:07:59,646
It's good to see you, man.

194
00:07:59,646 --> 00:08:01,106
Yeah, you, too.

195
00:08:01,106 --> 00:08:02,690
Man, so, what
are you up to?

196
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:04,859
I'm a commodities broker.

197
00:08:04,859 --> 00:08:07,154
Really? Yeah,
that-that sounds interesting.

198
00:08:07,154 --> 00:08:08,447
Yeah, it's not.

199
00:08:08,447 --> 00:08:09,656
Oh.

200
00:08:09,656 --> 00:08:10,991
But I'm rich and thin.

201
00:08:10,991 --> 00:08:13,368
Oh.

202
00:08:13,368 --> 00:08:14,953
Man, I don't think
I've seen you

203
00:08:14,953 --> 00:08:18,248
since Lance Davis's
graduation party.

204
00:08:18,248 --> 00:08:20,167
That was such
a fun night.
Yeah.

205
00:08:20,167 --> 00:08:21,668
Would have been good
if we'd gotten in

206
00:08:21,668 --> 00:08:23,337
but still, real fun.

207
00:08:23,337 --> 00:08:24,503
Yeah.
Yeah.

208
00:08:24,503 --> 00:08:26,006
God, we were
lame back then.

209
00:08:26,006 --> 00:08:27,799
Do you remember how
into dinosaurs we were?

210
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:33,347
Yeah.

211
00:08:33,347 --> 00:08:36,475
So, what do you...
what do you do now?

212
00:08:36,475 --> 00:08:38,435
So, how long
are you in town?

213
00:08:39,686 --> 00:08:41,313
Hi.

214
00:08:41,313 --> 00:08:42,605
MONICA:
Hey, sweetie.

215
00:08:42,605 --> 00:08:43,815
MONICA: Oh, good.
RACHEL: There you go.

216
00:08:43,815 --> 00:08:45,984
Rachel Green.

217
00:08:47,652 --> 00:08:48,987
Oh, oh,
that's right.

218
00:08:48,987 --> 00:08:50,613
Are you going
to be okay?

219
00:08:50,613 --> 00:08:52,740
Oh, I-I'll be fine.
It's just...

220
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:56,744
God, I hate her,
Ross. I hate her.

221
00:08:56,744 --> 00:08:58,497
Okay.

222
00:08:58,497 --> 00:09:01,166
Will, high school
was a long time ago.

223
00:09:01,166 --> 00:09:04,503
Look at her standing
there with those yams.

224
00:09:04,503 --> 00:09:06,338
My two greatest
enemies, Ross--

225
00:09:06,338 --> 00:09:08,589
Rachel Green and
complex carbohydrates.

226
00:09:11,343 --> 00:09:14,721
Oh, my God, Monica,
who is that?

227
00:09:14,721 --> 00:09:16,264
That's Will,
from high school.

228
00:09:16,264 --> 00:09:20,101
Oh. I do not remember him.

229
00:09:20,101 --> 00:09:24,105
Wow, really got that sexy,
smoldering thing going on.

230
00:09:29,694 --> 00:09:31,071
Oh, my God. He's...

231
00:09:31,071 --> 00:09:33,865
Look at the way
he's just staring at me.

232
00:09:33,865 --> 00:09:35,492
I think he's trying
to mouth something at me

233
00:09:35,492 --> 00:09:36,701
but I can't make it out.

234
00:09:40,579 --> 00:09:42,623
Okay, dinner's ready.

235
00:09:42,623 --> 00:09:43,875
Good game.
Yeah.

236
00:09:43,875 --> 00:09:46,586
Yeah, solid effort,
solid effort.

237
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:48,088
Oh, so who won?

238
00:09:48,088 --> 00:09:50,507
Green Bay.
Detroit.

239
00:09:50,507 --> 00:09:51,674
What?

240
00:09:51,674 --> 00:09:53,593
Well, the Lions
technically won

241
00:09:53,593 --> 00:09:57,097
but it was a moral victory
for the Green Bay... Mermen.

242
00:10:01,142 --> 00:10:02,310
Hi.

243
00:10:02,310 --> 00:10:03,686
Will, right?
Right.

244
00:10:03,686 --> 00:10:05,772
Right. Hi,
I'm Rachel Green.

245
00:10:05,772 --> 00:10:07,232
Oh, I remember you.

246
00:10:07,232 --> 00:10:08,316
Really?
Mm-hmm.

247
00:10:08,316 --> 00:10:10,777
Aren't you sweet?

248
00:10:10,777 --> 00:10:13,238
I got to tell you,
though, I am...

249
00:10:13,238 --> 00:10:16,241
I am having
the hardest time placing you.

250
00:10:16,241 --> 00:10:17,451
Oh, oh, hang on.

251
00:10:17,451 --> 00:10:19,160
I think I remember you.

252
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:20,870
Did we, um...

253
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:22,497
Did we fool around

254
00:10:22,497 --> 00:10:24,791
at Lance Davis's
graduation party?

255
00:10:24,791 --> 00:10:26,793
You are unbelievable.

256
00:10:26,793 --> 00:10:29,463
Thank you.

257
00:10:29,463 --> 00:10:30,547
Rachel, Rachel--

258
00:10:30,547 --> 00:10:31,839
why don't you
sit here?

259
00:10:31,839 --> 00:10:33,216
And, Will,
you sit way over there.

260
00:10:40,181 --> 00:10:41,349
